gahW(){return"How do I create or edit a project reminder?"},
gahj(){return"Only the owner can configure reminders, even if other members have the Admin role. Open project settings using the gear next to the project name in the calendar, choose Project reminders and press Add reminder. For a new project, save the project first."},
gahk(){return"Enter an internal name and the message to send. The notification shows the project name followed by Reminder and only the message. Choose the recurrence, days and delivery time, review the preview and press Save reminder. You can create several independent reminders. To change one, press Edit reminder on its card. Reminders are saved separately from the project form."},
gai2(){return"How do recurrence, delivery time and month-end dates work?"},
gahw(){return"Weekly lets you select one or more weekdays; Monthly lets you choose one or more days of the month. Each reminder uses one delivery time for all selected days. Create separate reminders for different delivery times. All times use Europe/Rome, even when your device is in another time zone."},
gahx(){return"If a selected day does not exist in a month, delivery uses the last available day. For example, the 31st becomes February 28 or 29. Selected days that coincide at month-end produce just one notification. Daylight saving changes are automatic: a nonexistent time in spring moves forward by the clock change; a repeated time in autumn uses standard time and produces only one delivery."},
gai1(){return"Who receives reminders? Can I include limited members?"},
gahu(){return"A reminder covers all project groups and includes the owner and non-limited members. Limited members are excluded by default: turn on Include limited members for that reminder to include them. Belonging to several groups does not multiply notifications on the same device; people with notifications enabled on several devices may receive one on each."},
gahv(){return"Deliveries use the members and roles already saved in the project, so save any changes to those details first. Each recipient must enable notifications on their own browser or device. The message uses the language written by the owner, without automatic translation."},
gai0(){return"How do I pause or delete a reminder?"},
gahs(){return"In the reminder list, turn off the switch on its card to pause deliveries. Its configuration stays saved, and you can turn it back on using the same switch: it resumes at the next future occurrence. To remove it, press Delete reminder and confirm."},
gaht(){return"Pausing, editing or deleting a reminder cancels its queued deliveries. A notification already being sent may still arrive; previously received notifications are not withdrawn. If you leave the editor without saving, you can choose to discard your changes."},
gai_(){return"Why is a reminder missing or late?"},
gahq(){return"Check that the reminder is active, that its days and Europe/Rome delivery time are correct and, for a limited member, that inclusion is enabled. The recipient must allow site notifications and complete device registration in Settings. While the app is open, the notification appears as a dialog; in the background it may appear as a system notification. Opening it takes you to the project calendar."},
gahr(){return"The delivery time is when sending is scheduled: the network, browser and device may delay receipt. After a service interruption, occurrences from the past hour may be recovered; older ones are skipped to avoid a burst of overdue notifications. If notifications still do not arrive, also check the question about enabling them."},
